---
system: sys-01-identity-household-access
flow_id: account-delete
surface: mobile
spec_anchor: /software/systems/01-identity-household-access#post-v1identityaccountdelete-request
actors: [ParentApp, Gateway, IdentityService, AccountDeletionService, SQS, SES, PostgreSQL]
apis:
  - POST /v1/identity/account/delete-request
  - GET /v1/identity/account/delete-status/{job_id}
externals: [SES]
queues: [SQS]
failure_paths:
  - pending_subscription_cancel_required
  - deletion_already_in_progress
  - retention_grace_period_active
idempotency: dedup on user_id — repeated request within grace period returns existing job_id
retry: caller-side exponential backoff with jitter on 5xx
timeout: 5s p99 for request; pipeline runs async over 30+ days
status: final
---
%% HAND-CURATED.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant ParentApp
    participant Gateway
    participant IdentityService
    participant AccountDeletionService
    participant SQS
    participant SES
    participant PostgreSQL

    Note over ParentApp,IdentityService: Entry point: parent_settings → Account → Delete Account — GDPR/COPPA deletion request

    ParentApp->>Gateway: POST /v1/identity/account/delete-request {confirm_phrase, reason?, X-Request-Id}
    Gateway->>Gateway: require valid parent JWT (ADR-0005 D6 — fresh within 60s)
    Gateway->>IdentityService: forward request
    alt pending_subscription_cancel_required
        IdentityService->>PostgreSQL: check active subscription state
        PostgreSQL-->>IdentityService: has_active_subscription=true
        IdentityService-->>Gateway: 409 pending_subscription_cancel_required {subscription_id}
        Gateway-->>ParentApp: 409 — parent must cancel subscription first
    else deletion_already_in_progress (dedup on user_id within grace period)
        IdentityService->>PostgreSQL: SELECT id, status, grace_period_ends_at FROM deletion_jobs WHERE user_id={user_id} AND status NOT IN ('completed','cancelled')
        PostgreSQL-->>IdentityService: existing_job
        IdentityService-->>Gateway: 200 {deletion_job_id: existing, status: in_grace_period, grace_period_ends_at}
        Gateway-->>ParentApp: 200 existing job returned
    else success
        IdentityService->>PostgreSQL: INSERT deletion_jobs {id, user_id, requested_at, grace_period_ends_at: now()+30d, status: in_grace_period}
        PostgreSQL-->>IdentityService: deletion_job_id
        IdentityService->>SQS: enqueue deletion_pipeline_trigger {deletion_job_id, user_id, execute_after: grace_period_ends_at}
        SQS-->>IdentityService: message_id
        IdentityService-)SES: (async) account_deletion_confirmation email {user_email, grace_period_ends_at, cancel_url}
        IdentityService-->>Gateway: 202 {deletion_job_id, status: in_grace_period, grace_period_ends_at, cancelable: true}
        Gateway-->>ParentApp: 202
    end

    Note over AccountDeletionService,SQS: --- Downstream async pipeline (after 30-day grace period) ---
    Note over AccountDeletionService,SQS: SQS message held until grace_period_ends_at; AccountDeletionService dequeues + executes full pipeline — see 14-retention/account-deletion-pipeline.sequence.mmd

    Note over ParentApp,IdentityService: --- Status poll ---

    ParentApp->>Gateway: GET /v1/identity/account/delete-status/{job_id}
    Gateway->>IdentityService: forward
    IdentityService->>PostgreSQL: SELECT status, grace_period_ends_at, completed_at FROM deletion_jobs WHERE id={job_id} AND user_id={caller_user_id}
    PostgreSQL-->>IdentityService: job record
    alt retention_grace_period_active
        IdentityService-->>Gateway: 200 {status: in_grace_period, grace_period_ends_at, cancelable: true}
        Gateway-->>ParentApp: 200
    else pipeline_running
        IdentityService-->>Gateway: 200 {status: pipeline_running, cancelable: false}
        Gateway-->>ParentApp: 200
    else completed
        IdentityService-->>Gateway: 200 {status: completed, completed_at}
        Gateway-->>ParentApp: 200
    end

    Note over ParentApp,PostgreSQL: timeout 5s p99 for sync path — pipeline executes async over 30+ days via AccountDeletionService — idempotent on user_id within grace period
